            <ArticleTitle>Complete Genome Sequence of a Novel Variant of Wenzhou Mammarenavirus.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01303-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01303-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Wenzhou mammarenavirus (WENV) is a novel species of Arenavirus that was first detected in China. We report here a novel WENV variant (WENV G107) from liver samples of Rattus norvegicus that shares 84.7% to 86.8% (large [L] segment) and 84.2% to 87.8% (small [S] segment) nucleotide sequence identity with its closest relative. The genomic characteristics were analyzed based on the whole genome of WENV G107.</AbstractText>
